Problem: Given the set \( A=\{1,2, \cdots, 10\} \). Define a function \( f: A \rightarrow A \) that satisfies:
(1) For any \( x, y \in A \), if \( x \leq y \), then \( f(x) \leq f(y) \);
(2) \( f(3)=4 \).
