We use the **"stars and bars"** method for this.

If we consider:

$$
\text{Number of non-decreasing sequences of length } n \text{ with values from } \{1, 2, \ldots, k\} = \binom{n + k - 1}{k - 1}
$$

This formula counts the number of **non-decreasing integer sequences of length $ n $ over the values $ \{1, 2, \ldots, k\} $**

Here:

